{title: This Is Our God (FJ_47_en)}
{song_number: 47}
{language: en}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[E]Your grace is enough, more than I need.
[C#m]At Your word [A]I will believe.
[E]I wait for You, [E/G#]draw me near again.
[C#m]Let Your Spirit [A]make me new.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And I will [A]fall at [B]Your [E/G#]feet,
I will fall [A]at Your [F#m]feet,
and I will wor[E/G#]ship You [A]here.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[E]Your presence in me, Jesus, light the way
[C#m]by the power [A]of Your word.
[E]I am restored, [E/G#]I am redeemed.
[C#m]By Your Spirit [A]I am free.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And I will [A]fall at [B]Your [E/G#]feet,
I will fall [A]at Your [F#m]feet,
and I will wor[E/G#]ship You [A]here.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[E]Freely You gave it all for us,
sur[B]rendered Your life upon that cross.
[F#m]Great is the love poured out for all:
[C#m]this is our [A]God.
[E]Lifted on high from death to life,
for[B]ever our God is glorified.
[F#m]Servant and King, [C#m]rescued the world:
[A]this is our [E]God.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus}
And I will [A]fall at [B]Your [E/G#]feet,
I will fall [A]at Your [F#m]feet,
and I will wor[E/G#]ship You [A]here.
{end_of_chorus}
